{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"reasoning","text":"Good. Use `lifecycleStatus: archived`.\n\nNow let me write the files. I'll start with the aggregation module and its .d.mts.\n\nLet me carefully write reliability-aggregation.mjs.\n\n```js\n/**\n * Deterministic reliability aggregation for the Agent Dev benefit report (E01).\n *\n * The module is a pure, dependency-free aggregator: it turns recorded trials\n * into the report columns E01 requires and never touches product behavior.\n * `pass^k` (a complete case whose k trials all pass) and `pass@k` (a complete\n * case with at least one passing trial) are separate, non-interchangeable\n * numbers. Incomplete cases carry an explicit reason and are excluded from the\n * denominator while staying visible in the report.\n */\n```\n\nFunctions:\n- `outcomeOf(trial)`\n- `isIncompleteOutcome`\n- `trialOutcome` \n- `classifyCase(entry, k)`\n- `aggregateReliability(input)`\n- `renderReliabilityMarkdown?` no.\n\nLet me write it fully and carefully.\n\n```js\nexport const INCOMPLETE_OUTCOMES = Object.freeze(['missing', 'timeout', 'crash', 'skip']);\nexport const DEFAULT_THRESHOLDS = Object.freeze({\n  k: 3,\n  minCases: 20,\n  flakeThreshold: 0.01,\n  safetySkipBudget: 0,\n  safetyFlakeBudget: 0,\n});\nexport const GATE_PASS = 'pass';\nexport const GATE_FAIL = 'fail';\nexport const GATE_INSUFFICIENT_SAMPLE = 'insufficient-sample';\n\nfunction isPositiveInteger(value) {\n  return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isInteger(value) && value > 0;\n}\n\nexport function normalizeThresholds(thresholds = {}, fallback = DEFAULT_THRESHOLDS) {\n  const k = thresholds.k ?? fallback.k;\n  const minCases = thresholds.minCases ?? fallback.minCases;\n  const flakeThreshold = thresholds.flakeThreshold ?? fallback.flakeThreshold;\n  const safetySkipBudget = thresholds.safetySkipBudget ?? fallback.safetySkipBudget ?? 0;\n  const safetyFlakeBudget = thresholds.safetyFlakeBudget ?? fallback.safetyFlakeBudget ?? 0;\n  if (!isPositiveInteger(k)) throw new TypeError(`reliability thresholds: k must be a positive integer, received ${JSON.stringify(thresholds.k)}`);\n  if (!isPositiveInteger(minCases)) throw new TypeError(...);\n  if (typeof flakeThreshold !== 'number' || !Number.isFinite(flakeThreshold) || flakeThreshold < 0 || flakeThreshold > 1) throw ...\n  if (!Number.isInteger(safetySkipBudget) || safetySkipBudget < 0) throw ...\n  if (!Number.isInteger(safetyFlakeBudget) || safetyFlakeBudget < 0) throw ...\n  return { k, minCases, flakeThreshold, safetySkipBudget, safetyFlakeBudget };\n}\n\nexport function outcomeOf(trial) {\n  if (typeof trial === 'string') return trial;\n  if (trial && typeof trial === 'object' && typeof trial.outcome === 'string') return trial.outcome;\n  return 'missing';\n}\n\nexport function isIncompleteOutcome(outcome) {\n  return INCOMPLETE_OUTCOMES.includes(outcome);\n}\n\nexport function trialResult(trial, expect) {\n  const outcome = outcomeOf(trial);\n  if (isIncompleteOutcome(outcome)) return 'incomplete';\n  return outcome === expect ? 'pass' : 'fail';\n}\n```\n\nclassifyCase(entry, k):\n```js\nexport function classifyCase(entry = {}, k = DEFAULT_THRESHOLDS.k) {\n  const id = typeof entry.id === 'string' && entry.id ? entry.id : null;\n  const kind = entry.kind === 'positive' || entry.kind === 'negative' ? entry.kind : 'coverage';\n  const expect = entry.expect === 'reject' ? 'reject' : 'accept';\n  const safety = entry.safety === true;\n  const scenario = typeof entry.scenario === 'string' ? entry.scenario : null;\n  const trials = Array.isArray(entry.trials) ? entry.trials : [];\n  const outcomes = trials.map(outcomeOf);\n  const results = outcomes.map(outcome => trialResult(outcome, expect));\n  const incompleteReasons = [];\n  if (trials.length < k) incompleteReasons.push('missing');\n  for (let index = 0; index < outcomes.length; index += 1) {\n    if (isIncompleteOutcome(outcomes[index]) && !incompleteReasons.includes(outcomes[index])) incompleteReasons.push(outcomes[index]);\n  }\n  const complete = incompleteReasons.length === 0;\n  const gateResults = results.slice(0, k);\n  const allPass = complete && gateResults.length >= k && gateResults.every(r => r === 'pass');\n  const anyPass = complete && gateResults.some(r => r === 'pass');\n  const firstTrialFailed = complete && results[0] === 'fail';\n  const flake = firstTrialFailed && results.slice(1).some(r => r === 'pass');\n  return { id, kind, expect, safety, scenario, complete, incompleteReasons, results, gateResults, allPass, anyPass, firstTrialFailed, flake };\n}\n```\n\nWait: `complete` requires results.length >= k AND no incomplete outcome. If trials.length >= k and no incomplete → complete. gateResults = first k. Since complete implies results.length >= k, gateResults.length === k. Good. Remove redundant check but keep for safety.\n\nNote `anyPass` requires complete.\n\nNow aggregate:\n\n```js\nexport function aggregateReliability(input = {}) {\n  const thresholds = normalizeThresholds(input.thresholds);\n  const { k } = thresholds;\n  const entries = Array.isArray(input.cases) ? input.cases : [];\n  const classified = entries.map(entry => classifyCase(entry, k));\n  const complete = classified.filter(c => c.complete);\n  const incomplete = classified.filter(c => !c.complete);\n  const denominator = complete.length;\n  const passedAll = complete.filter(c => c.allPass);\n  const passedAny = complete.filter(c => c.anyPass);\n  const flakeCases = complete.filter(c => c.flake);\n  const nonSafetyComplete = complete.filter(c => !c.safety);\n  const nonSafetyFlake = flakeCases.filter(c => !c.safety);\n  const safetyFlake = flakeCases.filter(c => c.safety);\n  const safetyCases = classified.filter(c => c.safety);\n  const safetyIncomplete = safetyCases.filter(c => !c.complete);\n  const safetyFailed = safetyCases.filter(c => c.complete && !c.allPass);\n  const positive = classified.filter(c => c.kind === 'positive');\n  const negative = classified.filter(c => c.kind === 'negative');\n  const positiveViolations = positive.filter(c => !(c.complete && c.allPass));\n  const negativeViolations = negative.filter(c => !(c.complete && c.allPass));\n  const byReason = countBy(incomplete.flatMap(c => c.incompleteReasons));\n  const perTrial = [];\n  for (let index = 0; index < k; index += 1) {\n    const evaluated = complete.length;\n    const passed = complete.filter(c => c.gateResults[index] === 'pass').length;\n    perTrial.push({ trial: index + 1, evaluated, passed, failed: evaluated - passed, successRate: evaluated === 0 ? null : passed / evaluated });\n  }\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nHmm perTrial: `evaluated` should be complete cases (all have gateResults length k). Good. Incomplete cases excluded.\n\nThen flake rate:\n```js\nconst nonSafetyFlakeRate = nonSafetyComplete.length === 0 ? null : nonSafetyFlake.length / nonSafetyComplete.length;\nconst flakeRate = denominator === 0 ? null : flakeCases.length / denominator;\n```\n\nGate reasons & status:\n```js\nconst reasons = [];\nif (positiveViolations.length) reasons.push(`positive-anchor-not-fully-satisfied: ${ids}`)\nif (negativeViolations.length) reasons.push(`negative-anchor-not-fully-rejected: ${ids}`)\nif (safetyIncomplete.length) reasons.push(`safety-case-incomplete: ${ids}`)\nif (safetyFlake.length) reasons.push(`safety-case-flake: ${ids}`)\nif (safetyFailed.length) reasons.push(`safety-case-failed: ${ids}`)\nif (nonSafetyFlakeRate !== null && nonSafetyFlakeRate > thresholds.flakeThreshold) reasons.push(`non-safety-flake-rate-above-threshold: ${rate} > ${threshold}`)\n```\nThen:\n```js\nlet gate;\nif (reasons.length > 0) gate = GATE_FAIL;\nelse if (denominator < thresholds.minCases) { gate = GATE_INSUFFICIENT_SAMPLE; reasons.push(`complete-cases-below-design-gate: ${denominator} < ${thresholds.minCases}`); }\nelse gate = GATE_PASS;\n```\nPass reasons: if gate === PASS add ['anchors-fully-satisfied','safety-zero-skip-zero-flake','non-safety-flake-within-budget','complete-cases-above-design-gate'].\n\nHmm mixing pass reasons with fail reasons is confusing; I'll always push a single explanatory `reason` list where each entry is a human sentence, and include `gate`. For clarity: when fail, reasons = violations; when insufficient, reasons = [below-design-gate]; when pass, reasons = [explanation]. Keep it simple: build `reasons` only for non-pass; and add `summary` string for all.\n\nLet me include `verdictNote`.\n\nAlso registry: if `input.knownScenarioIds`, compute referenced/unregistered.\n\nReturn:\n```js\n{\n  sampleId: input.sampleId ?? null,\n  expectation: input.expectGate ?? null,\n  matchesExpectation: input.expectGate ? gate === input.expectGate : null,\n  thresholds,\n  rawCaseCount: entries.length,\n  denominator,\n  passK: denominator ? { value: ..., count: passedAll.length, denominator } : { value: null, count: 0, denominator },\n  passAtK: {...},\n  perTrial,\n  flake: { count, cases: ids, firstTrialFailures: ids, rate: flakeRate, nonSafetyCount, nonSafetyRate, nonSafetyCases: ids, safetyCount, safetyCases: ids, threshold },\n  incomplete: { count, byReason, cases: [{id, scenario, reasons}] },\n  anchors: { positive: {total, satisfied, violating, violatingIds}, negative: {...} },\n  safety: { total, incompleteIds, flakeIds, failedIds, zeroSkip: safetyIncomplete.length===0, zeroFlake: safetyFlake.length===0 },\n  registry: {known, referenced, unregistered} | null,\n  gate,\n  reasons,\n  notes: [ 'pass^k and pass@k are reported separately and never mixed.', ... ],\n}\n```\n\nGood. Also expose `cases` detail? Might be big; include `cases: classified.map(summarize)` for transparency (\"在报告中保留\" incomplete cases). Yes include a trimmed per-case list: {id, scenario, kind, safety, complete, results, incompleteReasons, allPass, anyPass, flake, firstTrialFailed}. That satisfies \"保留首次失败\" and \"在报告中保留\" incomplete cases.\n\nOK. Now let me write it. I'll be careful with ESLint-ish cleanliness (though not linted).\n\nThen .d.mts declaring the same surface.\n\nLet's write."}}
