{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_103","type":"reasoning","text":"Now the fixture. I'll generate it with a Node script (deterministic), writing to shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json.\n\nBut first let me sanity-check the aggregator with a quick node smoke test using the module.\n\nThen build the fixture.\n\nFixture design (final):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"kind\": \"agent-dev-reliability-fixture\",\n  \"label\": \"deterministic-oracle\",\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"driven_by\": \"agent\",\n    \"source\": \"synthetic-local-deterministic-fixture\",\n    \"realProvider\": false,\n    \"realHuman\": false,\n    \"generalizationClaim\": false,\n    \"note\": \"Pre-registered deterministic oracle ... not a live provider or human result.\"\n  },\n  \"thresholds\": { \"k\": 3, \"minCases\": 20, \"flakeThreshold\": 0.01, \"safetySkipBudget\": 0, \"safetyFlakeBudget\": 0 },\n  \"scenarioRegistry\": \"shared/agent-dev/scenarios.ts\",\n  \"primarySample\": \"candidate\",\n  \"samples\": [ { id, description, expectGate, cases: [...] }, ... ]\n}\n```\n\nSample cases composition. Let me pick scenario ids from the registry: chat-empty, chat-streaming, models-heavy-usage, settings-provider-error, doctor-failed, gateway-connecting, knowledge-drafts, observability-trace-errors, transport-fallback-chain, skill-execution-timeout, multi-agent-handoff, knowledge-conflict-merge, channel-reconnect-storm, ui-v2-showcase.\n\ncandidate sample (24 complete + 4 incomplete):\n- positive anchors (6, 2 safety): all accept×3\n  - pos-chat-empty-render (safety)\n  - pos-chat-streaming-turn\n  - pos-models-usage-window\n  - pos-gateway-connecting-banner\n  - pos-knowledge-drafts-queue (safety)\n  - pos-observability-trace-errors\n- negative anchors (6, 2 safety): all reject×3\n  - neg-doctor-failed-payload (safety)\n  - neg-provider-error-surface\n  - neg-skill-timeout-budget (safety)\n  - neg-handoff-marker\n  - neg-conflict-merge-queue\n  - neg-channel-reconnect-storm\n- coverage (12):\n  - 8 all-pass\n  - 2 trial1 pass, trial2 fail, trial3 pass → allPass false, anyPass true, not flake (results[0] pass)\n  - 2 trial1 pass, trial2 pass, trial3 fail → allPass false, anyPass true\n  So passK = 16/24? Let's compute: positive 6 all pass + negative 6 all pass + coverage 8 all pass + 4 others (anyPass true, allPass false) = allPass 20, anyPass 24. passK = 20/24 = 0.833333; passAtK = 1.0.\n  Wait coverage has 12: 8 all-pass + 4 partial. Yes total complete = 6+6+12 = 24. allPass = 6+6+8 = 20. Good.\n- incomplete (4, non-safety coverage):\n  - inc-missing (trials: [\"accept\",\"accept\"] → length 2 < 3 → 'missing'; wait also \"missing\" outcome? Use trials length 2 → reason missing)\n  - inc-timeout ([\"accept\",\"accept\",\"timeout\"])\n  - inc-crash ([\"accept\",\"crash\",\"accept\"])\n  - inc-skip ([\"accept\",\"accept\",\"skip\"])\n  All non-safety.\n  \n  Hmm: inc-missing via short array yields reason 'missing'. Good.\n  \n  Note: these incomplete cases should not have kind positive/negative (they'd be anchor violations). Use kind 'coverage', safety false.\n\nperTrial for candidate: complete=24 → trial1 passed 24, trial2 passed 22 (4 partial cases: 2 fail at trial2, plus inc... no that's incomplete), trial3 passed 22. Let me compute: partial cases: c1 (pass,fail,pass), c2 (pass,fail,pass), c3 (pass,pass,fail), c4 (pass,pass,fail). trial1: all 24 pass. trial2: 22 pass. trial3: 22 pass. Good.\n\nflake for candidate = 0 → pass.\n\nSample \"insufficient-sample\": 8 complete healthy cases (2 pos, 2 neg, 4 coverage all pass) + 1 incomplete → denominator 8 < 20 → insufficient-sample. expectGate 'insufficient-sample'.\n\nSample \"anchor-not-satisfied\" (positive anchor violation): 20 complete: 5 pos (one with trial3 reject), 5 neg all reject, 10 coverage all accept. → gate fail. expectGate 'fail'.\n\nSample \"negative-anchor-not-rejected\": 20 complete: 5 pos all accept, 5 neg (one with trial2 accept), 10 coverage all accept → fail.\n\nSample \"safety-skip\": 20 complete healthy (4 pos incl 2 safety, 4 neg incl 2 safety, 12 coverage) + 1 safety case (kind positive? no—if it's positive it also violates positive anchor; that's fine but let's isolate: make the skipped safety case kind 'coverage' with safety true). Hmm, but \"安全必测项\" implies safety cases are typically anchors. To isolate the safety-incomplete rule, use a safety coverage case with a skip → gate fail due to safety-incomplete (not anchor). Good, isolates.\n  Wait but safety coverage case with skip also triggers... my gate: safetyIncomplete>0 → reason safety-case-incomplete. Yes isolated.\n  \nSample \"safety-flake\": 20 complete healthy + 1 safety coverage case with trials [\"reject\"?]... careful: for kind coverage expect='accept'. trials [\"reject\",\"accept\",\"accept\"] → trial1 fail, later pass → flake, safety → safety-flake reason. Also nonSafetyFlake unaffected. But also that case has allPass false. gate fail. Good.\n  Hmm, but if this safety case is kind coverage and also counts toward non-safety? No, it's safety. Good. The case is complete → denominator 21.\n  Also safetyFailed will include it (complete && !allPass) → extra reason. Fine, gate fail either way.\n\nSample \"flake-budget\": 24 complete: 20 healthy + 4 non-safety coverage cases with first-fail-then-rerun-pass (trials [\"reject\",\"accept\",\"accept\"] for expect accept → trial1 fail... wait expect is 'accept'; outcome 'reject' → result fail; then accept,accept → pass,pass → flake). 4 flake / 20 non-safety complete = 20% > 1% → fail. Good. Let me use 2 flake cases out of 22 → 9% > 1% → fail. Use 2 to keep smaller.\n\nLet me also consider adding a sample \"incomplete-retained\" demonstrating that incomplete cases are excluded but gate still passes with ≥20 complete — that's exactly the candidate sample. Good, no extra sample needed.\n\nSo 7 samples: candidate, insufficient-sample, anchor-not-satisfied, negative-anchor-not-rejected, safety-skip, safety-flake, flake-budget.\n\nNow let me write the generator. I'll generate with a node script inline (via node -e with a here-string to a temp .mjs file in $env:TEMP). Actually simplest: write the generator as a temp file in $env:TEMP via Set-Content, run node, then remove. But policy blocked Remove-Item earlier... it blocked a specific command; let me test removal of a temp file later. Alternatively keep the generator in .rsi/ (not part of targetScope but it's a hidden-ish dir; .rsi/TASK.json already lives there). Hmm, extra files in the repo could be flagged. Better: put generator in $env:TEMP.\n\nLet me write the generator to $env:TEMP/e01-fixture-gen.mjs using a PowerShell here-string with Set-Content -Encoding utf8 (this writes the JS; ASCII only). Then run `node $env:TEMP/e01-fixture-gen.mjs`.\n\nWait: does the fixture need only ASCII? Case ids ASCII. Yes.\n\nLet me write the generator.\n\nStructure of generator: helper functions:\n\n```js\nconst pass = ['accept','accept','accept'];\nconst rejectAll = ['reject','reject','reject'];\nfunction caseOf(id, scenario, kind, safety, trials, expect) { return { id, scenario, kind, expect: expect ?? (kind==='negative'?'reject':'accept'), safety, trials }; }\n```\n\nThen compose samples.\n\nLet me carefully enumerate scenarios used, cycling through registry ids.\n\nI'll write it now. Also include in fixture a `registry` note and `samples[].expectGate`.\n\nEmit with JSON.stringify(obj, null, 2) + '\\n'.\n\nLet me define case lists programmatically but with explicit per-case scenario assignment for realism.\n\nI'll write:\n\n```js\nconst pos = [\n  ['pos-chat-empty-render','chat-empty',true],\n  ['pos-chat-streaming-turn','chat-streaming',false],\n  ['pos-models-usage-window','models-heavy-usage',false],\n  ['pos-gateway-connecting-banner','gateway-connecting',false],\n  ['pos-knowledge-drafts-queue','knowledge-drafts',true],\n  ['pos-observability-trace-errors','observability-trace-errors',false],\n];\nconst neg = [\n  ['neg-doctor-failed-payload','doctor-failed',true],\n  ['neg-provider-error-surface','settings-provider-error',false],\n  ['neg-skill-timeout-budget','skill-execution-timeout',true],\n  ['neg-handoff-marker','multi-agent-handoff',false],\n  ['neg-conflict-merge-queue','knowledge-conflict-merge',false],\n  ['neg-channel-reconnect-storm','channel-reconnect-storm',false],\n];\nconst coverageAllPass = [...12 entries with scenarios...];\n```\n\nFor coverage I'll generate ids like cov-01..cov-12 with scenarios cycled.\n\nFor partial: cov-09..cov-12 partial.\n\nLet me lay out candidate:\n- positives 6 (all pass)\n- negatives 6 (all reject)\n- coverage 12: cov-01..cov-08 all accept; cov-09 (accept,reject,accept); cov-10 (accept,reject,accept); cov-11 (accept,accept,reject); cov-12 (accept,accept,reject)\n- incomplete 4: inc-missing (accept,accept), inc-timeout (accept,accept,timeout), inc-crash (accept,crash,accept), inc-skip (accept,accept,skip)\n\nTotal entries 28, complete 24.\n\ninsufficient-sample:\n- pos 2 (pos-...), neg 2, coverage 4 all pass, incomplete 1 (inc-timeout)\n→ complete 8.\n\nanchor-not-satisfied:\n- pos 5, with pos-03 trials (accept,accept,reject); neg 5 all reject; coverage 10 all accept → complete 20, positive violation → fail.\n\nnegative-anchor-not-rejected:\n- pos 5 all accept; neg 5 with neg-02 (reject,accept,reject); coverage 10 all accept.\n\nsafety-skip:\n- pos 4 (2 safety), neg 4 (2 safety), coverage 11 all accept (2 safety? no), plus safety-coverage-skip case kind coverage safety true trials (accept,accept,skip). Total entries 20, complete 19 (the skip one incomplete) → denominator 19 < 20! That would give insuffient-sample if no violation... but we have a violation (safety incomplete > budget 0) → fail. Fine. But to keep denominator >= 20, use 21 complete + 1 incomplete safety skip. Let me do: pos 5, neg 5, coverage 11 → 21 complete; plus safety coverage skip (incomplete) → denominator 21 ≥ 20 and safety violation → fail. \n\nsafety-flake:\n- pos 5, neg 5, coverage 11 all accept = 21 complete, plus safety coverage case with [\"reject\",\"accept\",\"accept\"] → complete, flake → 22 complete. Flake rate non-safety = 0; safety flake = 1 → fail (safety budget 0). \n\nflake-budget:\n- pos 5, neg 5, coverage 12: 10 all accept + 2 flaky non-safety ([\"reject\",\"accept\",\"accept\"]) → 22 complete, nonSafetyFlake=2, nonSafetyComplete=22 → rate 0.0909 > 0.01 → fail.\n\nGood. Now write the generator.\n\nAlso I should include in the fixture a couple of extra-RERUN cases (trials length 4) to test that reruns are handled? E.g., in flake-budget sample, one case with 4 trials [\"reject\",\"reject\",\"accept\",\"accept\"]. Nice to demonstrate reruns beyond k. Add one such case in flake-budget (making non-safety flake 3). Hmm keep it simple; but demonstrating >k trials is valuable for the \"fixed rerun\" semantics. I'll add one case with 4 trials in the flake-budget sample and note it. Actually the test file can construct synthetic cases for that. Keep fixture readable: I'll include one 4-trial case in candidate? No—candidate must have 0 flake. A 4-trial case with [\"accept\",\"reject\",\"accept\",\"accept\"] → result[0] pass → not flake, allPass false (gate trials: accept,reject,accept → not all pass), anyPass true. That adds a case with extra rerun and no flake. It changes candidate counts: complete 25, allPass 20, passAtK 25/25? Let me instead not add it to candidate to keep numbers clean... Actually it's fine and adds coverage of the \"rerun\" concept: passK = 20/25 = 0.8, passAtK = 1.0. Fine, and flake 0.\n\nHmm, but \"cov-13\" with 4 trials: trials = [\"accept\",\"reject\",\"accept\",\"accept\"]. Note gate trials = first 3 → accept,reject,accept → anyPass true, allPass false; results[0]='pass' → not flake. Good demonstration that a later rerun pass does NOT count as flake when the first trial passed. \n\nI'll add it to candidate. Then candidate: entries 29 (24 complete from before +1 = 25 complete, 4 incomplete) → wait recount: pos6+neg6+cov12+1(4-trial)=25 complete; incomplete 4 → total 29. passK=20/25=0.8, passAtK=25/25=1.0.\n\nLet me now generate. I'll write the generator file to $env:TEMP.\n\nActually simpler: I can write the fixture directly as a static JSON via apply_patch — but it's long. Generating is fine. Let me generate to a temp file then review before copying into the repo (to avoid publishing a broken file). I'll have the generator write to shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json directly and then review it.\n\nLet me write the generator.\n\nNote: PowerShell here-string content contains `$` maybe? Use single-quoted here-string to avoid interpolation.\n\nGenerator code:\n\n```js\nimport { writeFileSync, mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { dirname, resolve } from 'node:path';\n\nconst pass3 = ['accept','accept','accept'];\nconst reject3 = ['reject','reject','reject'];\n\nconst K = 3, MIN = 20, FLAKE = 0.01;\n\nfunction positive(id, scenario, safety, trials = pass3) { return { id, scenario, kind: 'positive', expect: 'accept', safety, trials }; }\nfunction negative(id, scenario, safety, trials = reject3) { return { id, scenario, kind: 'negative', expect: 'reject', safety, trials }; }\nfunction coverage(id, scenario, trials = pass3, safety = false) { return { id, scenario, kind: 'coverage', expect: 'accept', safety, trials }; }\n```\n\nThen build samples.\n\nLet me define reusable sets:\n\n```js\nconst POS5 = [\n  positive('pos-anchor-chat-empty','chat-empty', true),\n  positive('pos-anchor-chat-streaming','chat-streaming', false),\n  positive('pos-anchor-models-usage','models-heavy-usage', false),\n  positive('pos-anchor-gateway-connecting','gateway-connecting', false),\n  positive('pos-anchor-knowledge-drafts','knowledge-drafts', true),\n];\nconst NEG5 = [\n  negative('neg-anchor-doctor-failed','doctor-failed', true),\n  negative('neg-anchor-provider-error','settings-provider-error', false),\n  negative('neg-anchor-skill-timeout','skill-execution-timeout', true),\n  negative('neg-anchor-handoff-marker','multi-agent-handoff', false),\n  negative('neg-anchor-conflict-merge','knowledge-conflict-merge', false),\n];\nfunction cov(n) -> array of n coverage cases with cycled scenarios\n```\n\nSince JSON has no sharing, each sample gets fresh object copies (JSON.stringify duplicates anyway).\n\nScenario cycle list: ['ui-v2-showcase','chat-empty','chat-streaming','models-heavy-usage','settings-provider-error','doctor-failed','gateway-connecting','knowledge-drafts','observability-trace-errors','transport-fallback-chain','skill-execution-timeout','multi-agent-handoff','knowledge-conflict-merge','channel-reconnect-storm'].\n\nLet me write the generator with explicit construction, then verify counts by running the aggregator over it (self-check) and printing gate per sample.\n\nWrite generator to $env:TEMP\\e01-gen-fixture.mjs. Then run node.\n\nThen also verify with a node script that loads the fixture and aggregates each sample, printing gates vs expectGate.\n\nLet me do it in one command: create generator, run it, then run verification."}}
