{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_133","type":"reasoning","text":"Good pattern: `new URL('../../path', import.meta.url)`. I'll use that.\n\nNow write the test. Let me draft it.\n\n```ts\n// @vitest-environment node\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport {\n  aggregateReliability,\n  classifyCase,\n  DEFAULT_THRESHOLDS,\n  GATE_FAIL,\n  GATE_INSUFFICIENT_SAMPLE,\n  GATE_PASS,\n  INCOMPLETE_OUTCOMES,\n  normalizeThresholds,\n  trialResult,\n} from '../../scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs';\nimport type { ReliabilityCaseInput } from '../../scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs';\n\nconst fixture = JSON.parse(readFileSync(new URL('../../shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8'));\nconst registrySource = readFileSync(new URL('../../shared/agent-dev/scenarios.ts', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\nconst registeredScenarioIds = [...registrySource.matchAll(/\\{\\s*id:\\s*'([^']+)'/g)].map((match) => match[1]);\nconst benefitEvalSource = readFileSync(new URL('../../scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\n\nconst accept: ReliabilityCaseInput[] = ... helper\n\nfunction caseOf(id, kind, extra) {...}\n```\n\nHelpers to reduce verbosity:\n\n```ts\nconst accept3 = ['accept', 'accept', 'accept'];\nconst reject3 = ['reject', 'reject', 'reject'];\nfunction positive(id: string, safety = false, trials: string[] = accept3): ReliabilityCaseInput {\n  return { id, scenario: 'chat-empty', kind: 'positive', expect: 'accept', safety, trials };\n}\nfunction negative(id: string, safety = false, trials: string[] = reject3): ReliabilityCaseInput {\n  return { id, scenario: 'doctor-failed', kind: 'negative', expect: 'reject', safety, trials };\n}\nfunction coverage(id: string, trials: string[] = accept3, safety = false): ReliabilityCaseInput {\n  return { id, scenario: 'chat-streaming', kind: 'coverage', expect: 'accept', safety, trials };\n}\nfunction healthy(count: number): ReliabilityCaseInput[] {\n  return Array.from({length: count}, (_, i) => coverage(`cov-${i+1}`));\n}\n```\n\nTests:\n\ndescribe('thresholds'):\n- defaults\n- invalid throws\n\ndescribe('classification'):\n- trialResult pass/fail/incomplete\n- classifyCase short array → incomplete missing\n- classifyCase with 4 trials: gate uses first 3; rerun after first-pass isn't flake\n\ndescribe('pass^k vs pass@k'):\n- 4 cases: 2 all-pass, 2 partial → passK .5, passAtK 1; assert not equal and both separate fields\n\ndescribe('incomplete retention'):\n- cases incl missing/timeout/crash/skip → denominator excludes; incomplete.byReason; cases retained with reasons; gate insufficient-sample when below minCases... Let me construct 21 complete + 4 incomplete so gate=pass and check incomplete count/denominator.\n\ndescribe('flake'):\n- flaky case: first fail then rerun pass → flake count 1, allPass false (passK excludes), firstTrialFailed true, flake.cases includes id, firstFailureRetained true\n- non-flake: pass then fail later → flake 0\n- flake rate above threshold → gate fail\n\ndescribe('anchors & safety'):\n- positive violation → fail with reason containing id\n- negative violation → fail\n- safety skip with enough complete cases → fail (zeroSkip false)\n- safety flake → fail\n- healthy sample 20 complete → pass\n\ndescribe('insufficient sample'):\n- 19 complete → insufficient-sample; never pass\n- 0 cases → denominator 0, passK.value null, gate insufficient-sample\n\ndescribe('fixture oracle'):\n- thresholds match design gate (k=3,minCases=20)\n- primary sample exists & gate pass\n- every sample gate === expectGate\n- every case scenario registered\n- all four incomplete reasons appear in the fixture\n- provenance flags all false and driven_by agent\n\ndescribe('benefit report wiring'):\n- source includes \"aggregateReliability\" import and fixture path\n- the eval report artifact? Not available in a fresh run. Instead assert that buildReliability-equivalent aggregation over the fixture yields primary gate pass — already covered. I'll assert the source references.\n\nLet me be careful: `INCOMPLETE_OUTCOMES` equals ['missing','timeout','crash','skip'].\n\nLet me write it now. Also need `expect` name collision: I use a helper named `accept3` etc. Fine. Avoid naming a variable `expect`.\n\nWriting the file.\n\nNote: the `registry` regex `\\{\\s*id:\\s*'([^']+)'` matches the 15 real ids (agent-a/agent-b are `fromAgentId` so not matched). Good.\n\nAlso careful: test must not be named with `expect` shadowing.\n\nLet me write."}}
