rol-plane`? Let me check if a scenario spec with that id exists; if we set a scenario we must list its required rules/profiles. Simpler: no scenario field (like harness-gap-closure-plan.md which has no scenario... wait it has no `scenario` key indeed). Good.\n\nHmm, but is there a rule requiring task specs to declare a scenario? Only for gateway/plugin. OK.\n\nAlso `humanEvidence: not-required` — fine.\n\nNow `docs.required: true` and files → check-repository-artifacts will verify the doc is tracked; can't run here. Ok.\n\nRule spec: \n```yaml\n---\nid: reliability-aggregation-boundary\ntitle: Reliability aggregation stays a deterministic evidence report\ntype: ai-coding-rule\nseverity: error\n---\n\n- Reuse the existing agent-dev benefit report and scenario registry; do not add a parallel metrics platform or registry.\n- Pre-register k, minCases and the flake budget in the fixture before a run; never tune thresholds to the observed result.\n- Report pass^k (all k trials passed) and pass@k (at least one pass) as separate columns; never substitute one for the other.\n- Keep missing/timeout/crash/skip cases visible as incomplete, exclude them from the denominator, and never report them as healthy.\n- Keep the first trial failure when a fixed rerun succeeds; a rerun must not wash out the original gate failure.\n- Positive anchors must pass every trial and negative anchors must be rejected every time; safety cases allow zero skip and zero flake.\n- Below the design gate complete-case count, or without a safety/anchor violation, report insufficient-sample instead of PASS.\n- Label the fixture as a deterministic synthetic oracle (driven_by=agent); never claim a live provider, human verdict or generalization.\n- Do not change product defaults, product locks or approval semantics, and do not add scheduled automation.\n```\n\nNow the docs.\n\n3. docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e01-reliability-aggregation.md — Chinese narrative.\n\n4. docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e01-acceptance.json\n\n5. E01-SHA256SUMS\n\nLet me write the harness specs first.\n\nFor the acceptance list in the task spec, mirror the 8 AC in Chinese (concise).\n\nLet me write."}}
